I tested on Windows, with `\\` and `//`. (Vulkan + OpenGLES)
_The function `get_safe_dir_name` converts all `\` characters to `/`_

`ERR_PRINT("Can't create shader cache folder, no shader caching will happen: " + shader_cache_dir);
`

I think the safest change for all OS would be to simply replace `//` with `/`, in the function `OS::get_user_data_dir()`. `GLOBAL_GET` also considers `overrides`


```cpp
String OS::get_user_data_dir() const {
	String appname = get_safe_dir_name(GLOBAL_GET("application/config/name"));
	if (!appname.is_empty()) {
		bool use_custom_dir = GLOBAL_GET("application/config/use_custom_user_dir");
		if (use_custom_dir) {
			String custom_dir = get_safe_dir_name(GLOBAL_GET("application/config/custom_user_dir_name"), true);
			if (custom_dir.is_empty()) {
				custom_dir = appname;
			} else {
				custom_dir = custom_dir.replace("//", "/"); // <--- NEW
			}
```
